WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.042
Python lists are flexible general-purpose containers.

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:11.462
A list can hold different kinds of values, such as numbers, strings, and even other objects.

00:00:11.462 --> 00:00:19.239
NumPy arrays are designed mainly for numerical computing, and they usually contain values with the same data type.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:26.100
This difference allows NumPy to perform efficient mathematical operations across many values.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:32.645
For example, if we have an array of prices and want to increase every price by ten percent,

00:00:32.645 --> 00:00:36.610
we can multiply the entire array by one point one.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.865
We do not need to write a loop that updates each value separately.

00:00:40.865 --> 00:00:48.042
This style is called vectorized computation, and it is one of the most important ideas in numerical Python.
